.TH OBOUR 1 "2026-10-01" "Obour" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obour \- run apps from other Linux computers as windows on this desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obour
.br
.B obour
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Obour
opens apps that are installed on another Linux computer as normal windows on
your desktop, over SSH, with their sound on your speakers.
Wayland apps go through
.BR waypipe (1),
others through X11 forwarding.
.PP
Without a command, Obour opens its window.
The commands below work without it, for scripts and the terminal.
Wherever a command takes an
.IR app ,
give the app's id (see
.BR "obour list" )
or its name; the name must be unique, and case does not matter.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-json ]
Print each saved app: id, name, computer and command.
Apps in the app menu are marked
.BR [menu] .
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print every field of every app as JSON.
.TP
.B hosts
Print each computer that has saved apps, and how many.
.TP
.BI launch " app"
Start a saved app without opening the window, as app-menu entries do.
Problems are shown as desktop notifications.
.TP
.BI add " host command" " \fR[\fB\-\-name\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-menu\fR]"
Save an app that runs
.I command
on
.IR host ,
and print its new id.
.I host
is
.I user@host
or a
.B Host
from
.IR ~/.ssh/config .
Quote
.I command
if it has spaces.
The name defaults to the command's first word.
.B \-\-menu
also adds the app to this desktop's app menu.
Its settings start as
.IR inherit ;
change them in the window.
.TP
.BI remove " app"
Delete a saved app and its app-menu entry.
.TP
.BI backup " file.zip" " \fR[\fB\-\-with\-ssh\-key\fR]"
Save apps, computers, settings and app-menu entries to
.IR file.zip .
Passwords are never saved.
.B \-\-with\-ssh\-key
also saves your SSH key from
.IR ~/.ssh ;
keep that file private.
.TP
.BI restore " file.zip"
Replace apps, computers and settings with the backup's.
The current ones are kept in
.IR ~/.local/share/obour/backups .
.TP
.BR help " [" \fIcommand\fR ]
Show help for a command, or the list of commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help; after a command, that command's help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the app, file or computer could not be used,
2 when the command line is wrong.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/obour/
Saved apps
.RI ( launchers.json ),
computers
.RI ( hosts.json )
and settings
.RI ( settings.json ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/obour/
Icons, and the backups kept by
.BR restore .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/obour\-*.desktop
App-menu entries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
obour add me@server firefox \-\-menu
obour add laptop "gimp \-n" \-\-name "GIMP (laptop)"
obour launch firefox
obour list \-\-json | jq \-r '.[].name'
obour backup ~/obour.zip
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR waypipe (1),
.BR sshfs (1)
.PP
https://jazzmedo.github.io/Obour/
